// Custom library to be included as part of this extension. The contents of this file are appended to Raven's `Library` module.

// One functor, instantiated once per predicted type T, backing both prophecy
// flavors: `prophecyValue` (bound to `MultiTyp`, instantiated with a `List[T]`
// wrapper) for multi-shot prophecies, `prophecyValue1` (bound to `OneTyp`,
// instantiated with T directly) for one-shot ones. A prophecy only ever owns the
// one field matching how it was allocated -- the other sits unused, which is free
// in separation logic. Two independent parameters rather than one `Typ` reused as
// both `List[Typ]` and `Typ`: any field written as `List[Typ]` directly against a
// functor's own abstract parameter triggers a pre-existing bug in the
// module-instantiation/reification machinery (substitution renames qualified
// identifiers; it does not re-synthesize the auxiliary `Library.Type`-wrapper
// module `List[Typ]` needs, so that field's own `Frac$prophecyValue` datatype
// silently goes undeclared in the generated SMT for the instantiated module). A
// two-functor split (one module per flavor) avoids that but was tried first and
// rejected: it doubles the generic Frac/resource-algebra axiom schemas loaded into
// every verification's SMT context -- `--extension default` always loads this
// library -- which measurably slows down completely unrelated proofs. Keeping
// each field bound directly to its own bare parameter avoids both.
// The name of this module and these fields are hard-coded in
// prophecyExt.ml:ProphecyExt.ProphPredefs
module Prophecy[MultiTyp: Library.Type, OneTyp: Library.Type] {
    ghost field prophecyValue: MultiTyp
    ghost field prophecyValue1: OneTyp
}
